    {
      "id": "0F-H88H1jqKMGZQ6kgqW4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -72.52582118340115,
      "y": 163766.02309054043,
      "width": 1425.5999755859375,
      "height": 1305,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "_DQAZBjZXUbHhMMVtfkWx",
        "W-36s6-M6HHd4NcFFlnBx",
        "lvKmhc77LWNp0aQh0H3Gl",
        "sOIYCjcbdfwr-ktWs5hAd",
        "NFmtUbRcEYO0YXKX4M2nk",
        "zYUNU4bvULH9zo329jcTC"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c13X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1127970119,
      "version": 1109,
      "versionNonce": 1790245319,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789295513591,
      "created": 1789295502483,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "° The routes are also called \n\n        - Guardrails pipelines \n\n     and \n\n       - Presets\n\n° you can benefits from these preset pipelines of guradrailing\n\n        ==> So you can say: \n            - for preset A : use these sepecific detectors\n            - for preset B : use these specific detectors\n\n        ==> the gateway provides chat completions endpoints for\n            each of those presets\n\n        ==> The advantage of this is that you can hotswap in \n            different pipelines, different presets \n\n            and hotsawp between unguardrailed and guardrails models\n            without having to change any of your API contracts\n\n            So this lets you experiment really quickly between different\n            configurations of detectors\n                  - Experiment with how does the guardrail model\n                    perform compared to my own guardrailed model ?\n\n                  - Does it flag up the right queries ?",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "° The routes are also called \n\n        - Guardrails pipelines \n\n     and \n\n       - Presets\n\n° you can benefits from these preset pipelines of guradrailing\n\n        ==> So you can say: \n            - for preset A : use these sepecific detectors\n            - for preset B : use these specific detectors\n\n        ==> the gateway provides chat completions endpoints for\n            each of those presets\n\n        ==> The advantage of this is that you can hotswap in \n            different pipelines, different presets \n\n            and hotsawp between unguardrailed and guardrails models\n            without having to change any of your API contracts\n\n            So this lets you experiment really quickly between different\n            configurations of detectors\n                  - Experiment with how does the guardrail model\n                    perform compared to my own guardrailed model ?\n\n                  - Does it flag up the right queries ?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
